    "abstract": "Article history:                                    Let M be a compact Riemannian manifold equipped with a parallel differential form ω. We\nReceived 20 July 2009                               prove a version of the Kähler identities in this setting. This is used to show that the de\nReceived in revised form 8 January 2011             Rham algebra of M is weakly equivalent to its subquotient (Hc∗ (M ), d), called the pseudo-\nAccepted 25 January 2011\n                                                    cohomology of M. When M is compact and Kähler, and ω is its Kähler form, (Hc∗ (M ), d)\nAvailable online 2 February 2011\n                                                    is isomorphic to the cohomology algebra of M. This gives another proof of homotopy\n                                                    formality for Kähler manifolds, originally shown by Deligne, Griffiths, Morgan and Sullivan.\nKeywords:\nRational homotopy\n                                                    We compute Hc∗ (M ) for a compact G2 -manifold, showing that Hci (M ) ∼      = H i (M ) unless\nFormality                                           i = 3, 4. For i = 3, 4, we compute Hc∗ (M ) explicitly in terms of the first-order differential\nKähler identities                                   operator ∗d : 33 (M ) −→ 33 (M ).\nG2 -manifolds                                                                                            © 2011 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.",
